From f3207c77095114f9f2202ca7db8333d4c1a958d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuzhou Nie <rucnyz@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Apr 2026 13:31:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] screencasting: port SHM (memfd) fallback to upstream's
 damage-tracker refactor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Port of PR #1791 (wrvsrx/support-shm-sharing, 19 commits) onto upstream's
new screencasting architecture (commit 19866f8b "Refactor screencopy/screencast
to render via the damage tracker").

The original PR is currently dirty against upstream/main because both refactor
`dequeue_buffer_and_render` in conflicting ways. Rather than mechanically
rebasing the 19 commits, this single commit re-implements the SHM fallback on
top of the new architecture, preserving:

- Upstream's damage-tracker rendering on the DMA-BUF path (keeps FB cache).
- Upstream's element-slice cursor handling (cursor at start, sliced for
  metadata/hidden modes).
- All upstream behavior when the consumer accepts DMA-BUF — SHM only kicks in
  when PipeWire negotiates without a VideoModifier.

Changes vs upstream:

- New: `Shmbuf`, `SharingBuf`, `DmaNegotiationResult`, `allocate_shmbuf`,
  `render_to_shmbuf`, `clear_shmbuf`, `make_video_params_no_modifier`,
  `make_initial_params`.
- `CastInner` gains `shmbufs: HashMap<i64, Shmbuf>`.
- `CastState::ConfirmationPending`/`Ready` replace `modifier`+`plane_count`
  with `extra_negotiation_result: Option<DmaNegotiationResult>` (Some = DMA,
  None = SHM).
- Initial connect/update_params now offers an SHM (no-modifier) pod alongside
  DMA pods so consumers (Zoom, Feishu, etc.) that don't accept DMA-BUF can
  fall back.
- `param_changed` handles missing modifier as SHM negotiation.
- `add_buffer`/`remove_buffer` allocate/track DMA or SHM based on data type.
- `dequeue_buffer_and_render`/`_clear` route to the appropriate backend; SHM
  uses `render_and_download` (no FB cache, acceptable since SHM is fallback).
- `mark_buffer_as_good` -> `mark_buffer_after_render(_, _, SharingBuf)` so SHM
  can also stamp chunk.stride/offset.
